      {
        "y": 283.2,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 238.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Lobbying and petitioning"
      },
      {
        "y": 307.9,
        "x0": 148.4,
        "x1": 515.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "lobbying vary and can range from sending letters and making presentations to providingbriefing1briefing1"
      },
      {
        "y": 310.3,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 512.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Methods of lobbying vary and can range from sending letters, making presentations, providing material"
      },
      {
        "y": 319.9,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 498.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "material to Members and organisingrallies2 rallies2. Often the result lobbyists are seeking is for the MP or peer to"
      },
      {
        "y": 322.3,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 510.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to Members and organised . Often the result lobbyists are seeking for the MP or Lord to vote a certain way"
      },
      {
        "y": 331.9,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 502.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "vote a certain way on a specific issue. However,ultimatelythis decision3 downwill ultimatelyto4 3 be down to4 the MP or peer’s"
      },
      {
        "y": 334.3,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 511.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "on a specific issue. However, this decision will be the MP or Lord’s own judgement and the"
      },
      {
        "y": 344.9,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 423.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "owninfluencejudgement(if any) andthat theexistinginfluenceparty (ifpolicyany)willthathaveexistingon them.party policy will have on them."
      },
      {
        "y": 365,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 481.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 informational 2 large political meetings or demonstrations 3 in the end 4 the responsibility of"
      },
      {
        "y": 387.4,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 515,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The public can petition the House of Commons to make MPs aware of their opinion on an issue and to request"
      },
      {
        "y": 398.3,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 509.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "action. All that’s needed is that the petition is properly set out1 and has the signature and address of at least"
      },
      {
        "y": 411.4,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 504,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "one person. A petition can also be created and submitted online, as an e-petition. The text of the petition is"
      },
      {
        "y": 422.3,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 498.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "published in Hansard2. There is a procedure for petitions in the Lords, but it is very rarely used. Generally,"
      },
      {
        "y": 434.3,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 509.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "MPs will present3 all petitions they receive from their constituents4. MPs present petitions by either giving a"
      },
      {
        "y": 447.4,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 503.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "short statement in the debating chamber of the House of Commons or by simply placing the petition in the"
      },
      {
        "y": 458.3,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 513.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Petition Bag (which hangs behind the Speaker’s5 Chair). If a petition gets 100,000 signatures, the government"
      },
      {
        "y": 471.4,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 512.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "will respond and it will be considered for debate. A copy of the petition is sent to the appropriate government"
      },
      {
        "y": 482.3,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 499.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "department. Government departments are expected to offer observations6 on all substantive7 petitions."
      },
      {
        "y": 502.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 480.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 in the correct format 2 the official record of parliamentary business 3 make something known"
      },
      {
        "y": 514.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 502.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 people who voted for them, people in their constituency [political region] 5 MP with responsibility for"
      },
      {
        "y": 526.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 426,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "controlling the way parliamentary business is done 6 comments 7 of significance"
      },
      {
        "y": 544.6,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 203.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Select Committees"
      },
      {
        "y": 571.5,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 508.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "There is a Commons Select Committee for each government department, examining three aspects: spending,"
      },
      {
        "y": 582.5,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 506.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "policies1 and administration. Some Select Committees have a role that crosses departmental boundaries2,"
      },
      {
        "y": 594.5,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 515.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "such as the Environmental Audit3 Committee. Other Commons Committees are involved in a range of ongoing"
      },
      {
        "y": 606.5,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 498.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "investigations, such as allegations4 about the conduct5 of individual MPs. Lords Select Committees do not"
      },
      {
        "y": 618.5,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 515.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "shadow6 the work of government departments. Their investigations look into specialist subjects, taking advantage"
      },
      {
        "y": 630.5,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 513.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of the wide-ranging7 expertise8 of the Lords and the greater amount of time (compared to MPs) available to them"
      },
      {
        "y": 643.5,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 515.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to examine issues. Committees in the House of Lords concentrate on six main areas: international relations, the"
      },
      {
        "y": 654.5,
        "x0": 104.9,
        "x1": 490,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "European Union, science and technology, economic affairs, communications and the UK constitution9."
      },
      {
        "y": 675.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 510.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 official plans of action 2 deals with different departments 3 closely examines environmental consequences"
      },
      {
        "y": 686.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 516.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of government decisions 4 complaints that have not been proven 5 behaviour 6 follow closely to see how a"
      },
      {
        "y": 697.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 518.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "job is done 7 covering many subjects, diverse 8 high level of knowledge or skill 9 full set of laws of a country"
      }
